**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests`

**How to implement.** A fit's results report the rank of each solve's residual Jacobian, and the linear solves' results read the residual of their solution row by row (001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: … correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE'; the S11.4 brief 'the correlation matrix, the rank and the condition, through the MuellerInverse.ResidualJacobian carrier'). The carrier has the condition, the column norms and the correlation, but no rank. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`: `ResidualJacobian` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualJacobian`) gains, after `conditionNumber` (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`), `member this.rank : MatrixRank` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixRank`): the count of its singular values above 1.0e-6 times the largest, taken through the same `RealMatrix.create` seam and `Svd(false)` `conditionNumber` uses; `MatrixRank 0` for an empty Jacobian or one whose largest singular value is not above zero. Its doc says why the floor is relative and where it sits: two orders above the noise of a forward-difference Jacobian taken at ALGLIB's own step (about 1e-8 of a column), so two columns that agree only to that noise, an exactly confounded pair, count once, while a direction ten thousand times weaker than the strongest still counts. No other member of the carrier changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains, before `residualRmseAt` (step 352), `member this.residualsAt (solution : RealVector) : RealVector`: `RealMatrix.create` of its design rows' values times `solution`, less `RealVector.create` of `rhs`, the difference `residualRmseAt` takes the norm of; `residualRmseAt` becomes `(this.residualsAt solution).norm` over `sqrt` of the row count, the same operations in the same order, so the RMSE `createMathNetSvd` reports through it (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:createMathNetSvd`) and the product check's (step 352) are the same doubles. No other declaration of either file changes. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs`, `module FitResultsTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of S11.4's facts over the result shapes and synthetic least-squares problems: `a Jacobian's rank counts the directions its data constrains, above forward-difference noise`: the rank of `ResidualJacobian` of the rows [1; 0], [0; 1], [1; 1] is 2; of [1; 1], [2; 2], [3; 3] is 1; of [1; 1 + 1e-9], [2; 2 − 1e-9], [3; 3 + 2e-9] (columns proportional to a part in 1e9) is 1; of [1; 0], [0; 1e-4] is 2; and of no row is 0. `the residuals of a solution over a least-squares system are its design times the solution less its right-hand side`: the system of design rows [1; 0], [0; 1], [1; 1] and right-hand side [0.1; 2.1; 1.9] at the solution [0; 2] has `residualsAt` [−0.1; −0.1; 0.1] and `residualRmseAt` 0.1, each within 1e-15. `MuellerReconstructionTests` (the RMSE `createMathNetSvd` and the product check report) and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (the cheapest class reading a `ResidualJacobian`, through `residualJacobianAt`, step 336) run unchanged, their numbers bit-identical.

**Acceptance.** After the rank and the residuals land, `ResidualJacobian.rank` MUST count the singular values above 1.0e-6 of the largest and `LeastSquaresSystem.residualsAt` MUST answer A·x − b, the difference `residualRmseAt` reads; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a Jacobian's rank counts the directions its data constrains, above forward-difference noise` and `the residuals of a solution over a least-squares system are its design times the solution less its right-hand side`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` with their numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.
